<TrustPage
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How Havemoon selects topics, researches claims, uses sources, makes corrections, and separates editorial work from commercial interests."
>
  <h2>Editorial purpose</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon publishes practical English guidance for overseas buyers and importers working with
    China suppliers and manufacturers. Each page should help a reader understand or perform a
    defined task, not merely target a search phrase.
  </p>

  <h2>Research and sources</h2>
  <p>
    Operational guidance is based on documented sourcing, manufacturing, inspection, logistics, and
    supplier-management workflows. Claims about law, regulation, customs programs, official
    standards, or Incoterms are checked against primary sources whenever they are publicly
    available.
  </p>
  <p>
    Primary sources include regulators, customs authorities, legislation portals, standards or rule
    publishers, and official government guidance. Secondary commentary may help identify an issue
    but does not replace the controlling source.
  </p>

  <h2>Originality</h2>
  <p>
    Articles are written for Havemoon from a buyer-decision outline. The site does not reproduce
    supplier brochures, marketplace guides, other websites, or mass-generated article sets.
    Quotations are limited and attributed; the normal approach is original explanation and
    synthesis.
  </p>

  <h2>Review and update process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every guide has a publication date and may show a later update date.</li>
    <li>
      Time-sensitive compliance, customs, and program details are linked to current official pages.
    </li>
    <li>
      Material changes trigger a review of the affected explanation, checklist, and tool
      assumptions.
    </li>
    <li>
      When a page cannot determine a jurisdiction-specific answer, it says so and directs the reader
      to the proper authority or professional.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Independence and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial conclusions are not sold. Havemoon does not publish paid supplier rankings or treat a
    paid relationship as verification. If advertising or sponsored material is introduced later, it
    will be labeled and visually separated from editorial guidance.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of tools and automation</h2>
  <p>
    Research and editing tools may assist organization, consistency checks, and technical
    production. Publication responsibility remains with Havemoon. Pages are reviewed for usefulness,
    unsupported claims, source scope, internal consistency, and readability before release.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon provides general educational information, not legal, customs, tax, compliance,
    certification, or financial advice. Readers are responsible for confirming current requirements
    for their product, shipment, and jurisdiction.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
